<title>EGYPT: Egypt buys 110,000 t Australian wheat at $190/t.</title>
<headline>Egypt buys 110,000 t Australian wheat at $190/t.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Egyptian state's Holding Company for Rice and Flour Mills said it bought 110,000 tonnes of Australian hard wheat from the Australian wheat board at $190.00 a tonne C+F Egyptian Mediterranean ports.</p>
<p>The wheat is in two equal consignments -- 55,000 tonnes for shipment between February 10 and 28 and 55,000 tonnes for shipment between March 1 and 15, a company official said.</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Wright +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
